#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203852 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d6226fdb-ee73-5a78-87d5-9d6a988a9eb4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation With No Solutions"}] :question/id #uuid "fd07ad0f-548a-5569-84de-d658a88c4b9c" :question/math-academy-id "e-17087" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nI. $4z + 3 = 4z + 9$\n\nII. $2z - 5 = z + 1$\n\nIII. $3z - 2 = 3z - 2$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4z+3 & =4z+9 \\\\ 4z+3-4z & =4z+9-4z \\\\ 3 & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $z.$ Therefore, the equation $4z + 3 = 4z + 9$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2z-5 & =z+1 \\\\ 2z-5-z+5 & =z+1-z+5 \\\\ z & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $2z - 5 = z + 1$ has the unique solution $z = 6.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3z-2 & =3z-2 \\\\ 3z-2-3z & =3z-2-3z \\\\ -2 & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203853 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204090 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e7426e-553d-5f20-811f-15f3a5ea0056" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/id #uuid "cba9196c-fdc3-594d-a1ad-948cf75bd366" :question/math-academy-id "e-17213" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $y,$ given by\n\n$$\n4(r - 2)y = -8\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $r?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax = b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\neq 0.$ If $a = 0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ay = b.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na = 4(r - 2), \\qquad b = -8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n4(r - 2) = 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(r-2) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4(r-2)}{4} & =\\frac{0}{4} \\\\ r-2 & =0 \\\\ r & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203854 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204092 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/id #uuid "36eadc0b-c2b0-5f84-8f39-2b8399932edb" :question/math-academy-id "e-17214" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n2nx + 7  = -4x + 5\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $n?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax = b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\neq 0.$ If $a = 0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $ax = b.$ \n\nWe start by adding $4x$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2nx+7 & =-4x+5 \\\\ 2nx+4x+7 & =-4x+5+4x \\\\ 2nx+4x+7 & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we subtract $7$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2nx+4x+7 & =5 \\\\ 2nx+4x+7-7 & =5-7 \\\\ 2nx+4x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $x$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(2n + 4)x  = -2.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $ax = b{:}$\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{(2n + 4)}_{a}x  = \\underbrace{-2}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2n + 4= 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $n,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2n+4 & =0 \\\\ 2n+4-4 & =0-4 \\\\ 2n & =-4 \\\\ \\frac{2n}{2} & =\\frac{-4}{2} \\\\ n & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203878 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204091 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/id #uuid "5ee14499-89b0-59a3-9f13-b0a00c0e518d" :question/math-academy-id "e-18853" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $z,$ given by\n\n$$\n(r - 9)z + 2 = -1\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $r?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax = b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\neq 0.$ If $a = 0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $az = b{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-9)z+2 & =-1 \\\\ (r-9)z+2-2 & =-1-2 \\\\ {{(r-9)}_{⏟}}_{a}z & ={{-3}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nr - 9 = 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r-9 & =0 \\\\ r & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204596 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204090 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e7426e-553d-5f20-811f-15f3a5ea0056" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8639ce62-5e23-5361-b682-c7000582d54e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203491} {:answer/id #uuid "f6b1d5cd-7280-5a3b-b538-d976044c6e94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203492} {:answer/id #uuid "fcfa0123-90e9-5186-b54d-3ae7859972b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203493} {:answer/id #uuid "3cb6287c-2e23-513c-b813-c514eaaaaae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203494} {:answer/id #uuid "7dffe079-6e58-5eee-a2d4-f50f9c6c606c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8639ce62-5e23-5361-b682-c7000582d54e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203491} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9422b9e-c65d-596a-90ac-20fde363b97c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b6c453dd-3b6b-5f65-bf37-1fc261d1f26a" :question/math-academy-id "q-287665" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n2px=3\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=b.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=2p,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2p=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\np=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204597 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204091 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2937687-dedd-5964-bb4d-22153fc13d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2937687-dedd-5964-bb4d-22153fc13d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296297} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a06a891-d4f2-506a-bdd0-0692d7f6be31" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296775}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38670cb7-04d7-5bd3-bbc0-32b596369870" :question/math-academy-id "q-287667" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n2(p-4)x+2=5\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(p-4)x+2 & =5 \\\\ 2(p-4)x+2-2 & =5-2 \\\\ {{2(p-4)}_{⏟}}_{a}x & ={{3}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2(p-4)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(p-4) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(p-4)}{2} & =\\frac{0}{2} \\\\ p-4 & =0 \\\\ p & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d6226fdb-ee73-5a78-87d5-9d6a988a9eb4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation With No Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "533b9094-d677-5376-88f4-8f426a2a4cf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438046} {:answer/id #uuid "2b5a3d38-5a54-5a47-a0a8-64956fa7cdee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b5a3d38-5a54-5a47-a0a8-64956fa7cdee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438047} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd3eb9cd-0eda-53a6-bbc3-9f6bfbd15e06" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439052} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38767ef4-49fe-519a-b838-3b77b5b7521b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438048} {:answer/id #uuid "36138474-e8c9-5d26-acfa-e3b7ef2f057d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36138474-e8c9-5d26-acfa-e3b7ef2f057d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438049} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6d2fdbb-10bc-55e5-8c2c-6df645004975" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439053} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4435d623-199a-5d01-8347-ab72dc2191c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438050} {:answer/id #uuid "83476a1a-ee79-50fd-b7a1-580c8914eb50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4435d623-199a-5d01-8347-ab72dc2191c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438050} :answer-field/id #uuid "5259194c-9195-582d-b7ec-c468a67fa9be" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439054}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b892079-10a1-5d68-a34f-01695fac566e" :question/math-academy-id "q-288066" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $-3u+4=-3u-1$\n- **II.** $2u+5=2u+8$\n- **III.** $6u-2=3u+1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3u+4 & =-3u-1 \\\\ -3u+4+3u & =-3u-1+3u \\\\ 4 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $u.$ Therefore, the equation $-3u+4=-3u-1$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2u+5 & =2u+8 \\\\ 2u+5-2u & =2u+8-2u \\\\ 5 & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $u.$ Therefore, the equation $2u+5=2u+8$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6u-2 & =3u+1 \\\\ 6u-2-3u+2 & =3u+1-3u+2 \\\\ 3u & =3 \\\\ u & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $6u-2=3u+1$ has the unique solution $u=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508100 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d6226fdb-ee73-5a78-87d5-9d6a988a9eb4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation With No Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c78cb3d-2cc5-5e2c-9e55-a80e139339bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507616} {:answer/id #uuid "306bd0fa-00bf-5a91-966b-275a7a3521a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507663} {:answer/id #uuid "750f8f74-e77a-5d2e-8f3d-ca74279509fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507769} {:answer/id #uuid "b5b51887-d353-59f8-948b-51c3d03accf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507848} {:answer/id #uuid "b8fb200b-60c0-5f70-ae27-f8dd1334ced2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c78cb3d-2cc5-5e2c-9e55-a80e139339bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507616} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dd41eb7-fc07-5b0d-8a34-e949bc172ef0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507976}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d0bffce7-58da-5042-ae7f-fb5de551e1a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-288069" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nI. $2x-3=2x+4$\n\nII. $-5x+7=-2x-2$\n\nIII. $4x+1=4x+1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3 & =2x+4 \\\\ 2x-3-2x & =2x+4-2x \\\\ -3 & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $2x-3=2x+4$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5x+7 & =-2x-2 \\\\ -5x+7+2x-7 & =-2x-2+2x-7 \\\\ -3x & =-9 \\\\ x & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $-5x+7=-2x-2$ has the unique solution $x=3.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+1 & =4x+1 \\\\ 4x+1-4x & =4x+1-4x \\\\ 1 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204090 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e7426e-553d-5f20-811f-15f3a5ea0056" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27628a6f-5c23-5872-87a7-878f2e1da6b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507644} {:answer/id #uuid "4ba4ea7d-61a8-5364-be2d-d234f8cf3638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507713} {:answer/id #uuid "9bd678d9-2685-5d26-b56a-e4126c2c4ff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507816} {:answer/id #uuid "a039287f-5135-5191-970c-859892a6a41c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507823} {:answer/id #uuid "b5a20a9e-5f1a-5668-bd6f-c5fd978a900f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bd678d9-2685-5d26-b56a-e4126c2c4ff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507816} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa2138e2-b337-52b3-8a3d-5fd1ad2f1eba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508031}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6feec1bb-9d5b-5e0f-99d7-930f0577f85b" :question/math-academy-id "q-288107" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $t,$ given by\n\n$$\n5qt=-4\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $at=b.$ In this case,\n\n$$\na=5q,\\,b=-4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n5q=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\nq=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508108 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204091 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6b9eab8-ff3a-501f-9616-28e24c66aaf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6b9eab8-ff3a-501f-9616-28e24c66aaf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507931} :answer-field/id #uuid "11a9a15b-5aa0-5680-a061-a7bfedf60bfd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e39fec5d-501d-5ef0-88cc-5eeb84d919b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-288637" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $z,$ given by\n\n$$\n-7(k+3)z+8=1\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $az=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7(k+3)z+8 & =1 \\\\ -7(k+3)z+8-8 & =1-8 \\\\ {{-7(k+3)}_{⏟}}_{a}z & ={{-7}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n-7(k+3)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7(k+3) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{-7(k+3)}{-7} & =\\frac{0}{-7} \\\\ k+3 & =0 \\\\ k & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508045 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204091 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b304e2a-8f8e-5e89-a6a1-5c5b87fcc267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b304e2a-8f8e-5e89-a6a1-5c5b87fcc267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507684} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fdf80ca-384b-523b-a17d-5e97bc529c52" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f18d6f2-f26d-5ef1-84dd-3ecfcc80ad41" :question/math-academy-id "q-288639" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $v,$ given by\n\n$$\n2(q-7)v+5=1\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$\n\n$q=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $av=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(q-7)v+5 & =1 \\\\ 2(q-7)v+5-5 & =1-5 \\\\ {{2(q-7)}_{⏟}}_{a}v & ={{-4}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2(q-7)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(q-7) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(q-7)}{2} & =\\frac{0}{2} \\\\ q-7 & =0 \\\\ q & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204092 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ae663b6-85c5-5077-b87c-a6180d34333b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295510} {:answer/id #uuid "4b4fa932-686f-5272-80f1-319a4616fc55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295695} {:answer/id #uuid "5513a93f-ae93-5de6-bdce-765af89d5be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295759} {:answer/id #uuid "cdfab9aa-d797-5176-8659-fc606759afe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296346} {:answer/id #uuid "f950fb0f-6b6e-53ca-bbe7-61f27fce1157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdfab9aa-d797-5176-8659-fc606759afe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296346} :answer-field/id #uuid "1839f0af-c2f8-56ec-a3e2-a0f1a0ec6286" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6cf4ece6-fb8b-5a6f-963d-f97832f4331b" :question/math-academy-id "q-288662" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $y,$ given by\n\n$$\n3py=5y+8\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $ay=b.$ \n\nWe start by subtracting $5y$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3py & =5y+8 \\\\ 3py-5y & =5y+8-5y \\\\ 3py-5y & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $y$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(3p-5)y=8.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $ay=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(3p-5)}_{⏟}}_{a}y={{8}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n3p-5=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p-5 & =0 \\\\ 3p-5+5 & =0+5 \\\\ 3p & =5 \\\\ \\frac{3p}{3} & =\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ p & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297209 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204092 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38f1f5d0-a65b-50e5-ae53-71603b6a4f59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38f1f5d0-a65b-50e5-ae53-71603b6a4f59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295592} :answer-field/id #uuid "0392835c-e04b-5ad0-8c8d-d5dc8f5281c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93ece185-5396-5f04-8ab8-086b4b609861" :question/math-academy-id "q-288678" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $z,$ given by\n\n$$\n-3pz-8=-z-6\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $az=b.$ \n\nWe start by adding $z$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3pz-8 & =-z-6 \\\\ -3pz+z-8 & =-z-6+z \\\\ -3pz+z-8 & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we add $8$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3pz+z-8 & =-6 \\\\ -3pz+z-8+8 & =-6+8 \\\\ -3pz+z & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $z$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(-3p+1)z=2.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(-3p+1)}_{⏟}}_{a}z={{2}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n-3p+1=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3p+1 & =0 \\\\ -3p+1-1 & =0-1 \\\\ -3p & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{-3p}{-3} & =\\frac{-1}{-3} \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
